## 📖 Overview

**BHOC** is a **donor-independent, room-temperature-stable (3+ years), endotoxin-free, cell-antigen-free biologic hemoglobin oxygen carrier** designed for **microvascular and tissue-level oxygen exchange and delivery** across all mammalian species.

- ✅ Compatible with all blood types
- ✅ For all species — Companion and Wildlife animals
- ✅ 3–5× oxygen-carrying capacity vs. packed red blood cells (pRBCs)

---

## 🔬 Key Differentiators

| **Parameter** | **Traditional Blood** | **BHOC** |
|---------------|------------------------|----------|
| Donor Dependency | Required | **Eliminated** |
| Cross-matching | Required | **Not required** |
| Storage | Refrigerated (21–42 days) | **Room temperature (3+ years)** |
| Oxygen Efficiency | 1× (pRBCs) | **3–5×** |
| Wastage | 10–20% | **<2%** |
| Time to Deployment | 4–8 hours | **<3 minutes** |
| Species Compatibility | Donor-dependent | **Universal** |
| Hematocrit recovery | Need 5-6 days | **From 1 day** |

